1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:05,839
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,219 --> 00:00:14,347
[Diego] <i>Ivy, I saw Grandpa and</i>
<i>Arnaldo with their bodyguards.</i>

3
00:00:14,431 --> 00:00:17,976
<i>The congressman was just</i>
<i>forcing me on Arnaldo.</i>

4
00:00:18,059 --> 00:00:20,311
<i>Ivy, don't let him. I'll watch over you.</i>

5
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:22,689
<i>I'll do everything I can</i>
<i>to put an end to this.</i>

6
00:00:22,772 --> 00:00:25,483
<i>Why don't we conduct a survey?</i>

7
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:28,486
<i>Let's find out what</i>
<i>the public really thinks.</i>

8
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:30,947
[Julio] <i>We all know what</i>
<i>the public thinks, don't we?</i>

9
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:34,659
<i>That we, the Ardientes,</i>
<i>can still be trusted.</i>

10
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:36,536
[Arnaldo] <i>Ivy's right.</i>
<i>Better safe than sorry.</i>

11
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:38,705
[Loring] <i>We won the survey!</i>

12
00:00:38,788 --> 00:00:42,709
<i>Diego's got a shot as governor</i>
<i>of the new Ardiente!</i>

13
00:00:42,792 --> 00:00:44,210
[Arnaldo] <i>Should I get rid of Diego?</i>

14
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:48,089
[Julio] <i>Can you really kill</i>
<i>your own brother?</i>

15
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:51,009
<i>I want you to think carefully first.</i>

16
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:54,596
<i>Let's just say</i>
<i>this will be your initiation.</i>

17
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:58,099
<i>Through this, I will know</i>
<i>if you're just mad for power,</i>

18
00:00:58,183 --> 00:01:02,312
<i>or if you'll be a wise and good leader.</i>

19
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:06,191
<i>So, who is my father's killer?</i>
<i>Is it Emilia?</i>

20
00:01:06,274 --> 00:01:08,485
<i>Arnaldo? Or, is it you?</i>

21
00:01:08,568 --> 00:01:13,364
<i>Even though I never got the chance</i>
<i>to marry and have kids,</i>

22
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:16,409
<i>at least I was given a chance</i>
<i>to be a mother to you.</i>

23
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:20,914
<i>You complete me. Remember that, okay?</i>

24
00:01:20,997 --> 00:01:23,416
[Emilia] <i>Ivy is just playing you.</i>

25
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:26,878
<i>Who knows? She's with Diego,</i>
<i>the star of the survey.</i>

26
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:32,842
<i>What you should do is go to Ivy</i>
<i>to see just who she's flirting with.</i>

27
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:34,928
<i>The only thing I can promise you</i>
<i>is that nothing will change.</i>

28
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:37,430
<i>Lily will always be there for you.</i>

29
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:43,812
-You okay, sir?
-Sir?

30
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:50,235
-Sir, are you okay?
-I'm fine! Just stay there.

31
00:01:51,402 --> 00:01:52,403
Sir.

32
00:01:54,739 --> 00:01:56,116
-[grunts]
-Sir, calm down.

33
00:01:56,199 --> 00:01:58,076
-Sir, please stop.
-We're sorry.

34
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:01,079
Sir.

35
00:02:01,162 --> 00:02:04,040
-Sir, I'll help you.
-I said I'm fine!

36
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:05,792
Stop pestering me!

37
00:02:06,751 --> 00:02:10,922
[grunting]

38
00:02:11,005 --> 00:02:13,049
-Bro, back off.
-Sir, that's enough.

39
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:15,802
Sir, please stop.

40
00:02:24,435 --> 00:02:26,646
-How much wine did you drink?
-[laughing]

41
00:02:26,729 --> 00:02:29,399
Oh, come on. [laughing]

42
00:02:30,608 --> 00:02:32,068
I'll be fine.

43
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:35,029
I'll take these off, Nanny.

44
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:39,450
Thank you, Ivy.

45
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:44,038
And thank you for everything.

46
00:02:45,665 --> 00:02:47,292
-Go to sleep now.
-[chuckles softly]

47
00:02:48,835 --> 00:02:49,794
Dear.

48
00:02:52,964 --> 00:02:54,048
Come here.

49
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:01,097
Promise me…

50
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,893
that whatever happens,

51
00:03:04,976 --> 00:03:06,728
you'll always be happy.

52
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:12,609
I promise.

53
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,656
I love you.

54
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:25,079
I love you too.

55
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:33,713
Go to sleep now.

56
00:03:33,796 --> 00:03:34,964
Okay.

57
00:03:35,048 --> 00:03:40,053
[soft music playing]

58
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:04,035
Morning.

59
00:04:04,118 --> 00:04:09,123
[dark music playing]

60
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:13,836
Look at the headline.

61
00:04:17,006 --> 00:04:19,050
How did they find out about this?

62
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:23,972
I was wondering the same thing.

63
00:04:24,722 --> 00:04:26,516
You said you called for a news block--

64
00:04:26,599 --> 00:04:29,143
-I did! I told you I did!
-What is it doing there?!

65
00:04:31,771 --> 00:04:34,357
You were probably too drunk
that you don't even remember

66
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:36,651
what you did and what you didn't.

67
00:04:37,026 --> 00:04:38,695
-I'll fix this.
-Never mind.

68
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:41,572
I took care of it.

69
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:45,201
Front page material?

70
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:46,661
Damn!

71
00:04:54,794 --> 00:04:55,920
-Good morning.
-What is it?

72
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:57,839
There's a letter for you from--

73
00:04:57,922 --> 00:04:59,716
-I'm not expecting any--
-You have a letter.

74
00:04:59,799 --> 00:05:00,717
It's from…

75
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:04,304
[suspenseful music playing]

76
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:05,388
[gunshot]

77
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:09,475
[dramatic music playing]

78
00:05:13,396 --> 00:05:18,401
[melancholic music playing]

79
00:05:24,741 --> 00:05:26,159
Oh, Diego.

80
00:05:26,242 --> 00:05:28,036
What are you doing here?

81
00:05:28,119 --> 00:05:29,662
Good day, Miss Camia.

82
00:05:29,746 --> 00:05:32,165
Ivy asked me to accompany you here.

83
00:05:32,790 --> 00:05:36,169
I cleaned up a little
and I brought flowers too.

84
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:40,298
Diego, thank you.

85
00:05:40,923 --> 00:05:42,341
Oh. Let me get that.

86
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:55,396
[melancholic music playing]

87
00:06:02,779 --> 00:06:03,946
Hon…

88
00:06:06,574 --> 00:06:07,867
I really miss you.

89
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:11,579
I'm so sorry I didn't come sooner.

90
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:19,462
[melancholic music playing]

91
00:06:43,569 --> 00:06:45,780
Dante, I promise

92
00:06:45,863 --> 00:06:47,782
your death won't be in vain.

93
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:54,539
Lily and I will continue what you started.

94
00:06:56,249 --> 00:06:58,501
The Ardientes will go to jail, Dante.

95
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:01,254
They'll pay for everything…

96
00:07:02,421 --> 00:07:04,507
they've done to the people.

97
00:07:06,008 --> 00:07:11,013
[melancholic music playing]

98
00:07:24,318 --> 00:07:30,825
You can't leave until you
tell me who killed my father.

99
00:07:31,909 --> 00:07:33,411
First, show me the money.

100
00:07:34,662 --> 00:07:39,667
[sinister music playing]

101
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:49,844
Is this enough for you?

102
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:53,806
Now, tell me.

103
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:57,268
Who had my father killed?

104
00:07:58,686 --> 00:08:03,608
[sinister music playing]

105
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:08,279
Emilia.

106
00:08:10,990 --> 00:08:12,867
Emilia had him killed.

107
00:08:16,579 --> 00:08:18,748
[screams]

108
00:08:18,831 --> 00:08:20,500
I'll kill her!

109
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:22,335
[screams]

110
00:08:22,418 --> 00:08:25,338
She needs to pay! [breathing heavily]

111
00:08:25,421 --> 00:08:26,422
Natalie.

112
00:08:27,548 --> 00:08:29,800
If you want to kill Emilia,

113
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:31,177
you need to plan for it.

114
00:08:32,386 --> 00:08:34,680
Then set the appointment

115
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:36,474
between me and Emilia.

116
00:08:37,475 --> 00:08:42,063
Tell her somebody wants to meet her.

117
00:08:49,445 --> 00:08:50,863
This should be enough.

118
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:54,242
[suspenseful music playing]

119
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:56,494
Just set the damn meeting!

120
00:09:04,418 --> 00:09:08,130
Diego, thank you so much
for coming with me here.

121
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:10,383
No problem.

122
00:09:11,133 --> 00:09:12,301
You know…

123
00:09:13,803 --> 00:09:16,222
I treat you and Mister Dante
like my real parents.

124
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:21,310
That's why you shouldn't
call me Mrs. Camia anymore.

125
00:09:22,311 --> 00:09:24,397
Just call me Aunt Camia, okay?

126
00:09:25,648 --> 00:09:27,191
Okay, Aunt Camia.

127
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:30,152
-Okay, I'll go now.
-Take care.

128
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:32,113
-You too.
-[phone rings]

129
00:09:35,783 --> 00:09:36,867
Hello?

130
00:09:38,828 --> 00:09:41,831
You know the river Arthur was thrown in?

131
00:09:42,832 --> 00:09:44,667
Okay. I'll go there now.

132
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:47,753
Aunt Camia, I'll go with you.

133
00:09:48,546 --> 00:09:49,714
Okay, Diego.

134
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:02,727
Nanny Carlotta?

135
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:04,312
[Carlotta] I'll be right there, dear.

136
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:06,772
[phone rings]

137
00:10:08,858 --> 00:10:09,817
Mom?

138
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:13,779
[suspenseful music playing]

139
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:15,031
They have?

140
00:10:15,781 --> 00:10:17,450
Okay, Mom. I'll follow you there.

141
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:23,664
Nanny, I need to leave again.

142
00:10:23,748 --> 00:10:26,250
They found a lead on Arthur's whereabouts.

143
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:29,837
I'll be back soon.

144
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:32,298
Okay, dear.

145
00:10:33,966 --> 00:10:34,925
Ivy?

146
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:37,136
Nanny?

147
00:10:40,931 --> 00:10:42,183
Take care.

148
00:10:43,267 --> 00:10:47,438
[tender music playing]

149
00:10:58,449 --> 00:10:59,617
Thank you.

150
00:11:02,536 --> 00:11:03,537
Bye.

151
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:05,122
Wait, I'll see you out.

152
00:11:05,206 --> 00:11:06,957
[chuckles]

153
00:11:08,376 --> 00:11:11,170
-Bye, Nanny.
-Bye, dear. Take care!

154
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:21,138
I'm glad you wore the suit I gave you.

155
00:11:21,222 --> 00:11:22,515
It fits you.

156
00:11:22,598 --> 00:11:23,766
Oh, by the way.

157
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:28,896
Where are your cufflinks
with your initials?

158
00:11:29,563 --> 00:11:30,940
You should wear that.

159
00:11:31,023 --> 00:11:33,234
You know, this is
a very important meeting.

160
00:11:33,317 --> 00:11:34,735
[phone rings]

161
00:11:38,489 --> 00:11:39,323
Yes?

162
00:11:40,491 --> 00:11:41,742
Mission accomplished?

163
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:44,912
Until next time, then.

164
00:11:48,249 --> 00:11:49,333
[exhales deeply]

165
00:11:50,751 --> 00:11:51,877
You see, Arnaldo.

166
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:54,630
This can't go on.

167
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:57,508
I can't always be around

168
00:11:57,591 --> 00:12:00,261
to fix your mess every time you screw up.

169
00:12:01,554 --> 00:12:03,139
What's going on with you?

170
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:07,184
You're so obsessed with Miss Aguas

171
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:08,978
that you can't even
think straight anymore.

172
00:12:09,061 --> 00:12:10,229
[utensils clatter]

173
00:12:11,313 --> 00:12:12,440
Where are you going?

174
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:15,943
Ivy will be mine,
whether she likes it or not.

175
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:20,948
[dramatic music playing]

176
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:27,037
Women can really make men crazy.

177
00:12:30,916 --> 00:12:31,709
Ma'am.

178
00:12:34,503 --> 00:12:36,380
We found the drum open,

179
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:38,757
but there's no trace of the man
you're looking for.

180
00:12:38,841 --> 00:12:40,759
But we did find this piece of cloth.

181
00:12:41,802 --> 00:12:44,805
There's a big possibility that
Arthur escaped from the drum.

182
00:12:48,434 --> 00:12:52,313
[eerie music playing]

183
00:12:57,943 --> 00:13:00,404
[Arthur moaning]

184
00:13:07,953 --> 00:13:10,331
[Arthur moaning]

185
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:17,713
[eerie music playing]

186
00:13:22,718 --> 00:13:24,845
[breathing heavily]

187
00:13:26,972 --> 00:13:29,767
[breathing heavily]

188
00:13:43,364 --> 00:13:45,783
-[grunting]
-[thud]

189
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:49,787
[screaming]

190
00:13:54,333 --> 00:13:56,168
[breathing heavily]

191
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:06,220
[screams]

192
00:14:07,263 --> 00:14:10,099
[hyperventilating]

193
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:14,186
Calm down.

194
00:14:24,822 --> 00:14:26,240
Oh, no!

195
00:14:26,699 --> 00:14:28,367
She left her phone!

196
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:32,454
[ominous music playing]

197
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:35,583
[doorbell rings]

198
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:41,005
Ivy! [banging]

199
00:14:41,797 --> 00:14:43,424
Goodness! What now?

200
00:14:43,507 --> 00:14:44,925
Ivy!

201
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:46,802
Yes, Mr. Mayor?

202
00:14:47,261 --> 00:14:48,470
Where's Ivy?

203
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:50,180
She left, sir. She went out.

204
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:54,602
-[grunts] Mr. Mayor!
-Ivy!

205
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:55,769
Mr. Mayor, wait!

206
00:14:55,853 --> 00:14:58,731
-Ivy!
-Mr. Mayor, she's not here!

207
00:14:59,231 --> 00:15:01,609
And now you're trespassing!

208
00:15:06,822 --> 00:15:08,157
She's not here?

209
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:10,326
Ivy isn't here, sir.

210
00:15:10,409 --> 00:15:15,456
[suspenseful music playing]

211
00:15:17,791 --> 00:15:19,627
Then why is her cell phone here?

212
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:20,920
Mr. Mayor, she left it behi--

213
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:23,172
-Liar! [smacks]
-[groans]

214
00:15:34,725 --> 00:15:35,893
Ivy!

215
00:15:36,435 --> 00:15:38,687
-Sir!
-[gunshot]

216
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:40,022
-Sir!
-[Carlotta screams]

217
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:41,106
[gunshot]

218
00:15:42,608 --> 00:15:43,859
Sir, don't!

219
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:53,035
Ivy!

220
00:15:53,118 --> 00:15:54,411
Ivy, get down here!

221
00:15:58,123 --> 00:15:59,291
Ivy!

222
00:15:59,375 --> 00:16:03,379
[suspenseful music playing]

223
00:16:04,838 --> 00:16:06,090
Ivy!

224
00:16:11,762 --> 00:16:12,721
Ivy!

225
00:16:12,805 --> 00:16:17,810
[suspenseful music playing]

226
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:26,610
Ivy, get out of there! Open the door!

227
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:32,783
Ivy, open the door!

228
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:40,332
[banging]

229
00:16:40,416 --> 00:16:45,462
[suspenseful music playing]

230
00:16:49,883 --> 00:16:52,261
[ringing]

231
00:16:55,389 --> 00:16:57,891
Ivy. This is your number, right?

232
00:16:57,975 --> 00:16:59,727
[line ringing]

233
00:17:00,394 --> 00:17:03,772
Maybe it's Nanny Carlotta.
I left my phone with her. May I?

234
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:08,193
-Nanny?
-Ivy…

235
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:10,320
Ivy, the…

236
00:17:10,404 --> 00:17:11,238
Nanny?

237
00:17:13,782 --> 00:17:14,783
Nanny!

238
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:18,662
[gasps]

239
00:17:18,746 --> 00:17:19,747
Ivy--

240
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:23,834
-[dial tone]
-Nanny?

241
00:17:28,505 --> 00:17:30,591
I think something happened
to Nanny Carlotta.

242
00:17:30,674 --> 00:17:32,509
Garcia, take us home. Hurry.

243
00:17:32,593 --> 00:17:37,598
[suspenseful music playing]

244
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:43,187
[screams]

245
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:44,980
-[grunts]
-[shatters]

246
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:48,358
[groaning]

247
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:50,986
[screams]

248
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:55,199
[thud]

249
00:17:55,282 --> 00:17:57,993
-[groaning]
-[gasping]

250
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:09,546
[screams]

251
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:13,509
-[grunts]
-[choking]

252
00:18:14,551 --> 00:18:17,763
-[gasping]
-[groaning]

253
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:21,850
[screaming]

254
00:18:24,061 --> 00:18:25,562
[choking]

255
00:18:25,646 --> 00:18:30,651
[sinister music playing]

256
00:18:43,789 --> 00:18:48,794
[sinister music playing]

257
00:19:27,207 --> 00:19:32,212
[sinister music playing]

258
00:19:59,615 --> 00:20:02,618
Mayor, your grandpa wants
to talk to you in his office.

259
00:20:02,701 --> 00:20:03,702
Mayor?

260
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:09,416
Arnaldo.

261
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:12,336
Where have you been?

262
00:20:14,796 --> 00:20:17,382
Arnaldo! I'm talking to you.

263
00:20:17,466 --> 00:20:22,471
[tense music playing]

264
00:20:28,936 --> 00:20:31,688
Nanny Carlotta? Nanny?

265
00:20:32,814 --> 00:20:37,945
[tense music playing]

266
00:21:01,134 --> 00:21:02,594
[screams]

267
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:09,142
[wailing]

268
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:24,658
[screaming]

269
00:21:27,786 --> 00:21:30,580
[wailing]

270
00:21:39,506 --> 00:21:43,593
Who did this to you?!

271
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:47,973
Tell me!?

272
00:21:49,474 --> 00:21:52,436
[wailing]

273
00:21:58,483 --> 00:22:02,321
Who did this?!

274
00:22:10,871 --> 00:22:15,876
[dark music playing]

275
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:22,382
Who did this to you?!

276
00:22:27,929 --> 00:22:32,934
[dark music playing]

277
00:23:01,254 --> 00:23:03,715
[Arnaldo] <i>Gather the evidence,</i>
<i>and put them in the car.</i>

278
00:23:03,799 --> 00:23:05,050
<i>We'll burn everything.</i>

279
00:23:14,559 --> 00:23:17,187
<i>After that, put everything</i>
<i>back in its place.</i>

280
00:23:18,897 --> 00:23:21,483
<i>If you mess up, I'll kill you too.</i>

281
00:23:21,566 --> 00:23:26,655
[dark music playing]

282
00:23:46,716 --> 00:23:51,721
[brooding music playing]

283
00:24:23,962 --> 00:24:28,967
[brooding music playing]

284
00:25:22,312 --> 00:25:23,897
Burn this.

285
00:25:24,648 --> 00:25:25,941
Burn it, sir?

286
00:25:26,441 --> 00:25:27,943
Are you deaf or stupid?

287
00:25:28,443 --> 00:25:29,819
Burn it now!

288
00:25:29,903 --> 00:25:32,364
I'm sorry, Mayor. I'll burn it right away.

289
00:25:36,243 --> 00:25:37,327
Arnaldo.

290
00:25:39,746 --> 00:25:43,875
I feel like a broken record
trying to call you.

291
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:45,835
You've been ignoring me.

292
00:25:47,712 --> 00:25:49,547
Are you really trying to insult me?

293
00:25:49,631 --> 00:25:51,466
No, Grandpa. I didn't hear you.

294
00:25:51,549 --> 00:25:52,759
Liar.

295
00:25:53,635 --> 00:25:54,886
Admit it.

296
00:25:55,553 --> 00:25:58,723
You're playing deaf because
you did something wrong.

297
00:25:58,807 --> 00:26:02,811
[unsettling music playing]

298
00:26:22,539 --> 00:26:23,748
What do you mean?

299
00:26:24,791 --> 00:26:28,628
I heard you canceled
your meeting with our allies.

300
00:26:29,087 --> 00:26:30,005
To top it off,

301
00:26:30,088 --> 00:26:32,924
you didn't show up to
the campaign rally at the plaza.

302
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:36,177
Now tell me, what the hell
is happening to you?

303
00:26:36,261 --> 00:26:38,388
Why are you neglecting your job?

304
00:26:39,931 --> 00:26:41,808
I had something to take care of.

305
00:26:42,559 --> 00:26:43,810
With who?

306
00:26:44,144 --> 00:26:46,271
Is it Ivy Aguas again?

307
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:49,691
I'm warning you, Arnaldo.

308
00:26:50,859 --> 00:26:54,029
Don't let that woman be a distraction.

309
00:26:54,779 --> 00:26:56,197
Or else,

310
00:26:56,823 --> 00:26:58,575
I'll have her killed.

311
00:27:00,660 --> 00:27:04,456
We ran into some problems,
Grandpa, but I fixed them.

312
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:06,291
Like I always do.

313
00:27:07,751 --> 00:27:09,461
You have nothing to worry about.

314
00:27:13,465 --> 00:27:14,507
Excuse me.

315
00:27:22,849 --> 00:27:24,100
We'll see.

316
00:27:28,688 --> 00:27:29,856
Aunt Camia.

317
00:27:30,357 --> 00:27:32,734
I'm sorry, but you need to leave.

318
00:27:33,401 --> 00:27:36,112
The police are coming.
You can't be seen here.

319
00:27:36,571 --> 00:27:37,781
Diego…

320
00:27:38,406 --> 00:27:41,659
I don't think I can leave
Lily in this condition.

321
00:27:42,577 --> 00:27:44,662
Aunt Camia, I'll take care of Ivy.

322
00:27:45,163 --> 00:27:46,873
You need to go home.

323
00:27:46,956 --> 00:27:48,333
Mom, it's okay.

324
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:52,921
Please take her home.

325
00:27:57,425 --> 00:27:59,803
Keep me posted, okay?

326
00:28:00,345 --> 00:28:03,056
Don't worry. I'll take care of Ivy.

327
00:28:03,681 --> 00:28:04,933
Thank you, Diego.

328
00:28:37,340 --> 00:28:39,384
Mayor, we threw the corpses

329
00:28:39,467 --> 00:28:42,554
of Miss Aguas' bodyguards into the river.

330
00:28:42,637 --> 00:28:43,722
Good.

331
00:28:44,514 --> 00:28:46,599
Make sure you did a clean job

332
00:28:46,683 --> 00:28:48,476
so the police won't find any evidence.

333
00:28:50,103 --> 00:28:51,438
-Yes, Mayor.
-You can go.

334
00:29:03,783 --> 00:29:06,119
[police officer] We can't find
any signs of foul play.

335
00:29:06,202 --> 00:29:07,871
It looks like a case of suicide,
Miss Aguas.

336
00:29:10,206 --> 00:29:13,251
This wasn't suicide. She was murdered.

337
00:29:13,334 --> 00:29:16,379
Maybe she was going through
a financial problem,

338
00:29:16,463 --> 00:29:18,047
or maybe a relationship problem.

339
00:29:18,131 --> 00:29:20,175
-No.
-Are you sure?

340
00:29:20,258 --> 00:29:22,302
Maybe she was hiding something?

341
00:29:24,262 --> 00:29:25,680
Yes, I'm sure.

342
00:29:26,931 --> 00:29:29,768
I was talking to her when
our call suddenly got cut off.

343
00:29:29,851 --> 00:29:31,811
That's why I'm sure she was murdered.

344
00:29:32,729 --> 00:29:34,564
Have you seen the marks on her neck?

345
00:29:34,647 --> 00:29:36,357
It was caused by the cloth
around her neck--

346
00:29:36,441 --> 00:29:37,859
I'm not stupid!

347
00:29:38,568 --> 00:29:40,528
-That's hard to prove, ma'am.
-She was strangled.

348
00:29:42,739 --> 00:29:44,324
You're cops, aren't you?

349
00:29:44,407 --> 00:29:46,868
Why don't you search
every inch of my house

350
00:29:46,951 --> 00:29:51,915
and look for evidence before you
start jumping to conclusions?

351
00:29:51,998 --> 00:29:55,502
[tense music playing]

352
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:17,857
Umali, what's that? Did you find anything?

353
00:30:18,691 --> 00:30:19,776
No, sir.

354
00:30:21,569 --> 00:30:23,404
I'll keep looking over here.

355
00:30:24,155 --> 00:30:25,323
Okay.

356
00:30:27,325 --> 00:30:29,953
Mayor, our agent wants to talk to you.

357
00:30:32,330 --> 00:30:33,498
Hello?

358
00:30:33,581 --> 00:30:35,792
<i>Hello, Mayor.</i>
<i>I cleaned up the crime scene.</i>

359
00:30:37,293 --> 00:30:38,920
They won't find any evidence.

360
00:30:40,255 --> 00:30:41,589
[exhales deeply]

361
00:30:41,673 --> 00:30:43,258
Good. You'll get a bonus.

362
00:30:46,135 --> 00:30:47,345
I'll get going, Mayor.

363
00:30:57,230 --> 00:30:58,773
Good evening, Arnaldo.

364
00:30:59,858 --> 00:31:00,859
[grunts]

365
00:31:02,819 --> 00:31:04,445
Good evening, Grandpa.

366
00:31:09,450 --> 00:31:11,119
I received a report…

367
00:31:12,120 --> 00:31:14,914
from a very reliable source…

368
00:31:18,793 --> 00:31:23,089
saying that Ivy Aguas'
nanny committed suicide.

369
00:31:26,301 --> 00:31:27,468
Is it true?

370
00:31:28,595 --> 00:31:30,889
I don't know. Why… Why are you asking me?

371
00:31:30,972 --> 00:31:32,056
Well…

372
00:31:32,140 --> 00:31:34,058
Because I know that…

373
00:31:34,517 --> 00:31:40,523
you know everything
that goes on in her life.

374
00:31:44,694 --> 00:31:45,653
Well…

375
00:31:45,737 --> 00:31:47,238
I don't know anything about that.

376
00:31:49,115 --> 00:31:50,199
Arnaldo.

377
00:31:50,658 --> 00:31:52,994
Look at me straight in the eye.

378
00:31:56,456 --> 00:32:00,460
Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo.

379
00:32:02,211 --> 00:32:03,880
Don't try to fool me.

380
00:32:04,297 --> 00:32:06,883
I invented those tricks.

381
00:32:06,966 --> 00:32:07,884
Now…

382
00:32:09,052 --> 00:32:10,637
Tell me the truth.

383
00:32:11,846 --> 00:32:15,975
What do you know about the death
of Ivy Aguas' sweet old nanny?

384
00:32:21,898 --> 00:32:23,024
I killed her.

385
00:32:24,317 --> 00:32:28,279
[tense music playing]

386
00:32:31,741 --> 00:32:35,244
Ma'am, we couldn't retrieve any
footage from your CCTV cameras.

387
00:32:36,454 --> 00:32:38,289
Are you sure those are all working?

388
00:32:38,790 --> 00:32:40,875
My cameras aren't defective.

389
00:32:41,918 --> 00:32:44,712
I'm sure my CCTV cameras are working fine.

390
00:32:45,797 --> 00:32:48,299
You know what that murderer did?

391
00:32:48,967 --> 00:32:51,678
They wiped the crime scene clean

392
00:32:51,761 --> 00:32:55,223
to make it look like Nanny
Carlotta committed suicide.

393
00:32:55,306 --> 00:32:59,352
If I'm not mistaken,
they also killed my bodyguards.

394
00:32:59,435 --> 00:33:01,729
But, ma'am… If we can't find any evidence,

395
00:33:01,813 --> 00:33:03,439
all your suspicions are useless.

396
00:33:03,523 --> 00:33:05,566
You're the ones who are useless!

397
00:33:06,025 --> 00:33:08,778
You've been here for hours,
but you haven't found a thing!

398
00:33:08,861 --> 00:33:10,488
Get out of my house!

399
00:33:10,571 --> 00:33:14,367
You're all useless! Out! Now!
I want you out of my house!

400
00:33:14,450 --> 00:33:15,702
Just do what she says.

401
00:33:17,078 --> 00:33:22,083
[unsettling music playing]

402
00:33:25,044 --> 00:33:29,549
Stupid! Stupid! Stupid move.

403
00:33:33,886 --> 00:33:35,304
Are you an idiot?

404
00:33:36,514 --> 00:33:39,642
We are not maniacs.

405
00:33:40,518 --> 00:33:42,562
We don't just kill for no reason.

406
00:33:43,146 --> 00:33:45,773
We kill. Yes! We kill!

407
00:33:46,774 --> 00:33:48,776
But for a higher purpose.

408
00:33:50,069 --> 00:33:54,490
And that is to stay in power…

409
00:33:55,241 --> 00:33:57,702
for the sake of this town.

410
00:33:57,785 --> 00:33:59,162
And, most of all…

411
00:34:00,163 --> 00:34:01,706
for our family's sake!

412
00:34:03,916 --> 00:34:06,586
Ever since you entered politics,

413
00:34:06,669 --> 00:34:10,173
I did everything to protect you,

414
00:34:10,256 --> 00:34:12,341
to give you a good reputation.

415
00:34:13,468 --> 00:34:16,262
And, in a snap of a finger,

416
00:34:16,345 --> 00:34:17,764
you threw it all away

417
00:34:17,847 --> 00:34:21,017
for something that's not worth a damn!

418
00:34:22,018 --> 00:34:24,312
Arnaldo, why did you do this?!

419
00:34:24,395 --> 00:34:27,273
I mean… Will this do you any good?

420
00:34:27,356 --> 00:34:29,192
I don't know! I don't know!

421
00:34:29,859 --> 00:34:31,110
I didn't mean to do it!

422
00:34:31,778 --> 00:34:32,820
[snorts]

423
00:34:34,363 --> 00:34:36,074
I lost my temper!

424
00:34:36,157 --> 00:34:39,077
I went there because I learned
Diego's been pursuing Ivy.

425
00:34:39,160 --> 00:34:40,745
And Carlotta was there!

426
00:34:41,329 --> 00:34:43,539
She got in the way and tried to stop me.

427
00:34:43,623 --> 00:34:44,624
She kept pushing me!

428
00:34:44,707 --> 00:34:46,709
The next thing I know,
the bodyguards were there.

429
00:34:48,669 --> 00:34:50,963
And then… she was dead.

430
00:34:54,300 --> 00:34:56,803
She was dead. I… I didn't mean to do it.

431
00:35:01,599 --> 00:35:03,434
I… I didn't.

432
00:35:03,935 --> 00:35:05,686
This is all your fault.

433
00:35:06,979 --> 00:35:12,485
This is your fault for letting
that woman get into your head.

434
00:35:13,778 --> 00:35:18,449
You're ruining your future.

435
00:35:18,533 --> 00:35:21,786
All the perfect plans I laid out for you.

436
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:24,247
No.

437
00:35:26,499 --> 00:35:29,377
Nothing will be ruined
because I cleaned up my mess.

438
00:35:30,586 --> 00:35:33,798
I made sure that nobody
will find out I killed Carlotta.

439
00:35:33,881 --> 00:35:35,216
Not even Ivy.

440
00:35:37,176 --> 00:35:39,595
She can't find out because
she'll never forgive me,

441
00:35:39,679 --> 00:35:41,722
so I got rid of all the evidence.

442
00:35:41,806 --> 00:35:43,266
Nobody will find out what I did.

443
00:35:45,852 --> 00:35:48,187
I really hope so.

444
00:35:50,148 --> 00:35:51,440
No one will know.

445
00:35:58,948 --> 00:36:00,741
Ivy, I know what you're thinking.

446
00:36:02,034 --> 00:36:04,954
You know who's behind
Miss Carlotta's murder.

447
00:36:06,873 --> 00:36:08,291
The Ardientes.

448
00:36:09,750 --> 00:36:11,419
One of the Ardientes.

449
00:36:15,298 --> 00:36:17,341
Ivy, no matter what happens,

450
00:36:17,758 --> 00:36:19,635
I'll always be here for you.

451
00:36:20,970 --> 00:36:22,180
I'll help you.

452
00:36:22,471 --> 00:36:27,518
[dramatic music playing]

453
00:36:36,027 --> 00:36:41,032
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]

454
00:36:50,583 --> 00:36:53,211
<i>Thank goodness you're awake.</i>

455
00:36:53,878 --> 00:36:57,089
<i>I'm Carlotta, by the way.</i>

456
00:36:58,299 --> 00:37:05,306
<i>♪ And many times her eyes</i>
<i>Fought back the tears ♪</i>

457
00:37:06,474 --> 00:37:12,355
<i>♪ And when her youthful world</i>
<i>Was about to fall in ♪</i>

458
00:37:12,438 --> 00:37:15,691
<i>♪ Each time her slender shoulders ♪</i>

459
00:37:15,775 --> 00:37:19,195
<i>♪ Bore the weight of all her fears ♪</i>

460
00:37:19,278 --> 00:37:23,783
<i>♪ And a sorrow no one hears… ♪</i>

461
00:37:23,866 --> 00:37:26,118
<i>-Nanny Carlotta.</i>
<i>-I was so worried about you.</i>

462
00:37:26,202 --> 00:37:29,538
<i>I could not rest without you by my side.</i>

463
00:37:31,249 --> 00:37:33,584
<i>I want to stay here with you.</i>

464
00:37:33,668 --> 00:37:35,795
<i>I don't want anything bad</i>
<i>to happen to you.</i>

465
00:37:36,921 --> 00:37:40,758
<i>♪ Let her dream ♪</i>

466
00:37:40,841 --> 00:37:43,844
<i>♪ For she's a child ♪</i>

467
00:37:43,928 --> 00:37:50,893
<i>♪ Let the rain fall down upon her ♪</i>

468
00:37:50,977 --> 00:37:57,942
<i>♪ She's a free and gentle flower</i>
<i>Growing wild… ♪</i>

469
00:37:58,025 --> 00:37:59,193
[Carlotta] <i>You know,</i>

470
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:03,531
<i>even though I never got the chance</i>

471
00:38:03,614 --> 00:38:06,325
<i>to marry and have children,</i>

472
00:38:06,409 --> 00:38:09,578
<i>at least I was given a chance</i>
<i>to be a mother to you.</i>

473
00:38:09,662 --> 00:38:11,998
<i>You complete me, dear.</i>

474
00:38:13,624 --> 00:38:17,003
[Ivy] <i>Thank you for always being there.</i>

475
00:38:18,629 --> 00:38:22,049
<i>-I can do this, right?</i>
<i>-Yes, dear.</i>

476
00:38:27,513 --> 00:38:30,933
[crying]

477
00:38:42,236 --> 00:38:44,196
[Ivy] <i>I won't let the Ardientes hurt you.</i>

478
00:38:44,280 --> 00:38:46,615
<i>You're the only family I have.</i>

479
00:38:46,699 --> 00:38:50,619
<i>-I don't know what I'd do if--</i>
<i>-Calm down.</i>

480
00:38:50,703 --> 00:38:54,498
<i>All that anger won't do you any good.</i>

481
00:38:54,582 --> 00:38:56,250
<i>I won't leave you.</i>

482
00:38:59,503 --> 00:39:03,174
<i>Who did this to you?!</i>

483
00:39:04,800 --> 00:39:06,510
<i>Tell me?!</i>

484
00:39:10,389 --> 00:39:12,933
<i>♪ Let her cry ♪</i>

485
00:39:13,017 --> 00:39:17,229
<i>♪ For she's a lady ♪</i>

486
00:39:17,313 --> 00:39:20,858
<i>♪ Let her dream ♪</i>

487
00:39:20,941 --> 00:39:24,278
<i>♪ For she's a child ♪</i>

488
00:39:24,362 --> 00:39:31,369
<i>♪ Let the rain fall down upon her ♪</i>

489
00:39:31,452 --> 00:39:38,417
<i>♪ She's a free and gentle flower</i>
<i>Growing wild ♪</i>

490
00:39:38,501 --> 00:39:42,254
<i>♪ She's a free and gentle flower ♪</i>

491
00:39:42,338 --> 00:39:45,633
<i>♪ Growing wild ♪</i>

492
00:39:45,716 --> 00:39:49,303
<i>♪ She's a free and gentle flower ♪</i>

493
00:39:49,387 --> 00:39:53,849
<i>♪ Growing wild ♪</i>

494
00:39:57,019 --> 00:40:02,024
[tender music playing]

495
00:41:05,713 --> 00:41:10,718
[tender music playing]

496
00:41:26,192 --> 00:41:27,359
Diego.

497
00:41:38,287 --> 00:41:39,330
Thank you.

498
00:42:08,734 --> 00:42:10,236
Diego, any updates?

499
00:42:11,237 --> 00:42:13,656
The police haven't found any evidence yet.

500
00:42:14,156 --> 00:42:15,491
But Ivy thinks that the Ardientes

501
00:42:15,574 --> 00:42:18,577
-had something to do with it.
-[scoffs]

502
00:42:20,162 --> 00:42:22,957
I wouldn't be surprised
if that's the case.

503
00:42:24,416 --> 00:42:25,668
How's my daughter?

504
00:42:28,295 --> 00:42:29,421
She's distraught.

505
00:42:30,214 --> 00:42:32,132
She's been quiet.

506
00:42:32,633 --> 00:42:34,176
Were you with her all night?

507
00:42:38,973 --> 00:42:41,100
Diego, thank you.

508
00:42:41,934 --> 00:42:43,477
Thank you so much.

509
00:42:44,019 --> 00:42:47,064
I feel relieved knowing that
you're always there for Lily.

510
00:42:48,232 --> 00:42:50,192
I know you're having a hard time,

511
00:42:50,276 --> 00:42:52,820
but I hope you won't tire of loving her.

512
00:42:53,862 --> 00:42:57,032
Because you're one of the
important people in her life.

513
00:43:00,536 --> 00:43:02,621
I'm always here for Lily.

514
00:43:03,789 --> 00:43:07,835
Ever since we were kids,
I've been by her side.

515
00:43:10,504 --> 00:43:11,755
Thank you, Diego.

516
00:43:21,932 --> 00:43:23,100
[phone rings]

517
00:43:27,062 --> 00:43:28,272
Natalie.

518
00:43:28,355 --> 00:43:31,609
<i>Didn't I tell you not to</i>
<i>call me when I'm at home?</i>

519
00:43:32,192 --> 00:43:33,193
[sighs]

520
00:43:33,694 --> 00:43:34,820
Well…

521
00:43:36,196 --> 00:43:37,573
I'm bored.

522
00:43:37,906 --> 00:43:40,951
<i>Hmm. When are you going</i>
<i>to set the appointment</i>

523
00:43:41,035 --> 00:43:44,788
between me and your lovely wife?

524
00:43:46,373 --> 00:43:48,000
Natalie, listen to me.

525
00:43:48,459 --> 00:43:52,004
It's not the right time
for you to face Emilia yet.

526
00:43:52,546 --> 00:43:54,298
We need to carefully plan this.

527
00:43:54,798 --> 00:43:58,677
Okay. So, what's your plan?

528
00:44:03,015 --> 00:44:04,266
[giggles]

529
00:44:05,976 --> 00:44:10,981
[brooding music playing]

530
00:44:26,664 --> 00:44:28,082
<i>Nanny Carlotta.</i>

531
00:44:28,165 --> 00:44:32,086
<i>Please forgive me for not protecting you.</i>

532
00:44:32,169 --> 00:44:34,630
<i>You didn't deserve to die.</i>

533
00:44:44,765 --> 00:44:47,059
<i>They may have succeeded</i>
<i>in erasing the truth,</i>

534
00:44:47,142 --> 00:44:49,353
<i>but I have the perfect punishment in mind</i>

535
00:44:49,436 --> 00:44:52,564
<i>waiting for the person who killed you.</i>

536
00:44:52,648 --> 00:44:56,944
<i>And they can't erase it</i>
<i>no matter what they do.</i>

537
00:44:57,027 --> 00:45:02,032
[unsettling music playing]

538
00:45:05,744 --> 00:45:09,498
<i>Nanny, help me find</i>
<i>the monster who killed you.</i>

539
00:45:12,751 --> 00:45:17,881
<i>I won't let your killer</i>
<i>roam free, Nanny Carlotta.</i>

540
00:45:17,965 --> 00:45:21,885
<i>I'll find out who that person is</i>
<i>and make them pay.</i>

541
00:45:22,219 --> 00:45:27,224
[unsettling music playing]

542
00:45:37,651 --> 00:45:40,237
<i>-Bye.</i>
<i>-Wait. I'll see you out.</i>

543
00:45:40,320 --> 00:45:42,156
[chuckles]

544
00:45:43,574 --> 00:45:45,033
[Carlotta] <i>Oh, no!</i>

545
00:45:45,451 --> 00:45:46,869
<i>She left her phone!</i>

546
00:45:50,706 --> 00:45:51,957
[doorbell rings]

547
00:46:02,843 --> 00:46:07,848
[unsettling music playing]

548
00:46:51,975 --> 00:46:54,937
[screaming]

549
00:46:58,482 --> 00:47:01,026
[suspenseful music playing]

550
00:47:07,824 --> 00:47:12,829
[suspenseful music playing]

551
00:48:00,419 --> 00:48:04,798
[unsettling music playing]

552
00:48:11,430 --> 00:48:13,765
[Arnaldo screaming]

553
00:48:16,143 --> 00:48:19,313
[bleak instrumental playing]

554
00:48:42,085 --> 00:48:43,086
[suspenseful sting]

555
00:48:45,172 --> 00:48:47,090
<i>A-A-T.</i>

556
00:48:48,884 --> 00:48:50,260
<i>Arnaldo.</i>

557
00:48:51,053 --> 00:48:52,471
<i>Ardiente.</i>

558
00:48:53,013 --> 00:48:54,264
<i>Torillo.</i>

559
00:48:55,641 --> 00:49:01,146
<i>What do you have to do</i>
<i>with Nanny Carlotta's death?</i>

560
00:49:05,317 --> 00:49:08,737
[Ivy] <i>I wish I could dream</i>
<i>of Nanny Carlotta,</i>

561
00:49:08,820 --> 00:49:12,824
<i>and that she'd tell me</i>
<i>who did this to her.</i>

562
00:49:12,908 --> 00:49:14,117
<i>I don't trust her.</i>

563
00:49:14,201 --> 00:49:15,869
<i>Ivy's different. She's not like you.</i>

564
00:49:15,952 --> 00:49:17,037
[Emilia] <i>Can you just help me out?</i>

565
00:49:17,120 --> 00:49:20,540
<i>Let's convince Arnaldo</i>
<i>not to go on this trip with Ivy!</i>

566
00:49:20,624 --> 00:49:21,792
<i>-I'll convince him.</i>
<i>-Go on.</i>

567
00:49:21,875 --> 00:49:23,710
<i>What are you doing, Papa?!</i>

568
00:49:23,794 --> 00:49:26,254
[Julio] <i>You mean to tell me not</i>
<i>even a bullet in his head</i>

569
00:49:26,338 --> 00:49:29,591
<i>is going to convince him</i>
<i>to change his mind?!</i>

570
00:49:30,175 --> 00:49:31,510
[Ivy] <i>Mr. Mayor, I want you to choose</i>

571
00:49:31,593 --> 00:49:34,638
<i>which one of these</i>
<i>I should use to kill you.</i>

572
00:49:37,849 --> 00:49:40,977
[theme music playing]
